From d6c91bd932055902b12dd60cb3a8a422964ad201 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei Gosman <andrei.gosman@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:23:02 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] support: give unique_thread an 8 MB stack on Darwin

Linux threads get the RLIMIT_STACK default of 8 MB. Darwin gives
secondary threads 512 kB, and the FAPI messages the MAC and PHY
adaptors keep on the stack add up to more than that along the call
chain (a dl_tti_request is 74 kB, an ul_tti_request 34 kB, several per
slot): on the first slot after cell creation the gNB died with SIGBUS in
the stack probe (___chkstk_darwin) of
fapi_to_phy_fastpath_translator::send_dl_tti_request on a main_pool
worker.

Introduce detail::os_thread, the subset of std::thread that unique_thread
uses (join, joinable, get_id). On Darwin it creates the thread with
pthread_create and an explicit 8 MB stack and learns its std::thread::id
from the new thread itself, so callers that compare against
std::this_thread::get_id() keep working. On Linux it is std::thread, so
nothing changes there.
---
 .../ocudu/support/executors/unique_thread.h   | 71 +++++++++++++++++--
 lib/support/executors/unique_thread.cpp       | 65 +++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 126 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

